# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the tsan-system preset (B-20).
#
# Only frames inside libraries that are not built with -fsanitize=thread
# (Ubuntu's libLLVM, libclang-cpp, libsqlite3) may be listed here, each with
# the reason it is a false report. Never list a function of lcart: a race in
# lcart's own code is fixed, with a test.

# LLVM's statistic registry: TrackingStatistic::RegisterStatistic() takes a
# lock that is an llvm::ManagedStatic, created on first use with
# double-checked locking on a std::atomic<void*> (ManagedStatic.h). That
# atomic publication happens inside the uninstrumented libLLVM, so TSan sees
# the mutex allocated by one worker and locked by another with no ordering
# between them. Reported when two workers register their first statistic
# while parsing at the same time.
race:llvm::TrackingStatistic::RegisterStatistic
